  "preflight": "  [PREFLIGHT] pec_faces={z_lo} creates an INFINITE PEC boundary AND the geometry contains finite PEC objects. For antennas or finite-GP structures, the pec_faces boundary makes the ground plane cover the entire domain face, which changes the physics (cavity vs radiating antenna). If you need a finite ground plane, remove pec_faces and use an explicit PEC Box instead.\n  [PREFLIGHT] all dielectric(s) ['duroid'] are perfectly lossless in an open (CPML) domain. If you are measuring Q / resonance, this gives an ARTIFICIALLY infinite Q (design-guide Anti-Pattern #1, an R5 surface-metric trap) \u2014 add loss, e.g. sigma = 2*pi*f*eps0*eps_r*tan_delta. (Harmless if you are not measuring Q.)\n  [PREFLIGHT] MSL port 'p1' at x=2.50mm, direction='+x': distance to nearest x-CPML = 900\u00b5m < recommended 1588\u00b5m (= 2\u00b7h_sub). Source-side CPML reflection may inflate |S11|. Move port further from boundary OR increase domain x-extent.\n  [PREFLIGHT] MSL port 'p1' (direction='+x'): 3-probe V\u2083 at x=11.30mm sits 1166\u00b5m from a strong reflector (PEC Box at x\u2208[12.47,15.01]mm y\u2208[3.00,23.32]mm); recommended \u2265 1676\u00b5m (= \u03bb_g/4 at f_max with \u03b5_eff_proxy=5.0). Standing-wave content at the probes will bias `compute_msl_s_matrix`'s Z\u2080 extraction and |S11|@notch \u2014 physical |S11|\u21921 at a quarter-wave open stub may read as -5 to -10 dB instead of 0 dB.  Mitigation: extend L_LINE so the line between port and reflector is \u2265 \u03bb_g/2, OR bump n_probe_offset on add_msl_port to push V\u2083 further into a clean travelling-wave region.\n  [PREFLIGHT] MSL port 'p2' at x=24.97mm, direction='-x': distance to nearest x-CPML = 900\u00b5m < recommended 1588\u00b5m (= 2\u00b7h_sub). Source-side CPML reflection may inflate |S11|. Move port further from boundary OR increase domain x-extent.\n  [PREFLIGHT] MSL port 'p2' (direction='-x'): 3-probe V\u2083 at x=16.17mm sits 0\u00b5m from a strong reflector (PEC Box at x\u2208[15.01,27.47]mm y\u2208[15.26,17.67]mm); recommended \u2265 1676\u00b5m (= \u03bb_g/4 at f_max with \u03b5_eff_proxy=5.0). Standing-wave content at the probes will bias `compute_msl_s_matrix`'s Z\u2080 extraction and |S11|@notch \u2014 physical |S11|\u21921 at a quarter-wave open stub may read as -5 to -10 dB instead of 0 dB.  Mitigation: extend L_LINE so the line between port and reflector is \u2265 \u03bb_g/2, OR bump n_probe_offset on add_msl_port to push V\u2083 further into a clean travelling-wave region.\n"
